### DELETE /v1/matchmaking/tickets/{ticketId} — cancel a search
###
### When to use: when the player gives up searching for a match. Only accepted
### while the ticket is SEARCHING and belongs to the authenticated player —
### otherwise 409 or 403. The ticket is marked CANCELLED and removed from the
### Redis queue.
###
### How to use: run POST /v1/matchmaking/tickets first (captures `ticketId`),
### then run the request below.
###
### Expected: 200 with the ticket JSON (status: "CANCELLED").
### Error cases: unknown id → 404; other player's ticket → 403; not SEARCHING → 409.

@apiBaseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Happy path — expect 200 with status CANCELLED
DELETE {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error case — second cancel → expect 409
DELETE {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error case — unknown id → expect 404
DELETE {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/matchmaking/tickets/does-not-exist
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
